", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"260765e6c3b0e8f746ecb3e7bd1203735c34be88c141a7824ed753f3084615b1","event_uuid":"33cf76bf-6afe-46f2-9f88-b3b1d41a5a07","position":{"commit_sha":"bb9723f289404333238a2697efc7db6f5e370e82","position":"1787394538353717001-33cf76bf-6afe-46f2-9f88-b3b1d41a5a07"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"75aad24fa3950ea5683be5251512b6efbbce8e7038805d0ce780c35d9cce7415","event_uuid":"69c3c9b5-f154-4e31-bfbf-83d1c0eb6b87","position":{"commit_sha":"24a161535ee4617801b8c4660ea2ce3033edf4c4","position":"1787395536701097001-69c3c9b5-f154-4e31-bfbf-83d1c0eb6b87"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"e02849b1d7d957b74e3718d687f74e954f3609b40da62714d98b4399138117c0","event_uuid":"98b64f53-62ed-41a0-9be7-25aa12891fa8","position":{"commit_sha":"2e4762ecc087040fab342bca044af3531e77f8d8","position":"1787395543893930001-98b64f53-62ed-41a0-9be7-25aa12891fa8"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Decision: ADDED the leg (snapshot-gc-worker). Both design questions resolved: (1) staleness IS the shared table — gc_trigger acquires via rebar._store.stamped_lock.stamped_file_lock, which writes the v2 stamp and adjudicates via lock_owner.stamped_file_is_stale, so doctor's _existence_report is the right reader unchanged; (2) root derivation made READ-ONLY via new repo_snapshot.peek_store_root() + gc_trigger.worker_lock_probe_path() (store_root/_gc_dir mkdir as side effects; a diagnostic must not materialise an absent store — it reports the lock free). Doctor tests gain an autouse REBAR_GATE_TMPDIR pin because this is the census's one host-global probe. Pushed as Gerrit change 2099 (commit 3737dbd57a).","timestamp":1787389905760091001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Merged: Gerrit change 2099 → commit d6a2ea0d6c (LLM-Review +1, Verified +1). doctor's lock census now reports six legs; the snapshot-gc-worker leg derives its per-host path read-only and reports held-for/holder/staleness via the shared table, with tests for live holder, dead holder (stale finding) and absent store (free, store not created).","timestamp":1787394538353717001}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1787354646844370001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"c6f1c5de-cbac-4877-8942-abe5d06ced83","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"8a0d-96ca-a60e-4da6"},{"link_uuid":"149cb421-ad7d-4c43-8072-4ac094e9ea60","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"4a87-4da3-1a92-43a9"}],"description":"## Context\n\nDiscovered while adding the compact-worker leg to doctor's lock census (ticket\nbemused-painted-worm / 8a0d-96ca-a60e-4da6, merged as 8874ec98c7c). Snapshot GC's\noperation-linked trigger (a3da2f4cce) added a stamped worker lock at\n`<snapshot-store>/gc/worker.lock` (`rebar._snapshot.gc_trigger._WORKER_LOCK_NAME`), the same\ndetached-background-worker shape as `.rebar/compact-worker.lock` — a lock most likely to be\nheld by a process an operator cannot find with `ps`. `doctor_locks.scan_locks` censuses only\ntracker-adjacent locks, so a snapshot-GC worker that died between acquire and release leaves\na stamped lock the one diagnostic built to answer \"who holds what\" cannot see.\n\n## Decision\n\nADD the leg. The two design questions the ticket raised resolve cleanly:\n\n1. **Staleness discipline IS the shared table.** `gc_trigger._acquire_worker_lock` uses\n   `rebar._store.stamped_lock.stamped_file_lock` (the consolidation from story\n   1cf6-f902-5bfa-438f), which writes the same v2 ownership stamp as the drain and\n   compact-worker locks and adjudicates reclaim via\n   `rebar._store.lock_owner.stamped_file_is_stale`. So doctor's existing\n   `_existence_report` — which decodes the v2 stamp and asks that same shared table — is\n   exactly the right reader, no new staleness heuristic.\n2. **Root derivation must be READ-ONLY.** The lock lives on the per-host snapshot store\n   (`rebar._snapshot.repo_snapshot.store_root()`, `$REBAR_GATE_TMPDIR` or\n   `tempfile.gettempdir()`, dir `rebar-gate-snapshots`), NOT the tracker's `.rebar/`. But\n   `store_root()` mkdirs+chmods the root and `gc_trigger._gc_dir` mkdirs `<store>/gc/` as\n   side effects — a diagnostic pass must not create directories (the census's existing\n   read-only guarantee: probing must never create what it probes). So the leg needs a\n   non-creating derivation seam, added where each layer already owns its layout.\n\nA store that does not exist yet reports the leg `free` — for an existence lock the file IS\nthe lock, so an absent store trivially holds nothing; this matches how the drain and\ncompact-worker legs report an absent lock file, and the row's note says the store may not\nexist yet.\n\n## Approach\n\n1. `src/rebar/_snapshot/repo_snapshot.py`: add `peek_store_root() -> Path` — the same\n   base-resolution as `store_root()` (`config.resolve_gate_tmpdir()` or\n   `tempfile.gettempdir()`, joined with `_STORE_DIRNAME`) WITHOUT mkdir/chmod; refactor\n   `store_root()` to call it then create (behavior preserved).\n2. `src/rebar/_snapshot/gc_trigger.py`: hoist the `\"gc\"` dirname into a `_GC_DIRNAME`\n   constant used by `_gc_dir`, and add `worker_lock_probe_path() -> Path` returning\n   `peek_store_root() / _GC_DIRNAME / _WORKER_LOCK_NAME` with no directory creation —\n   gc_trigger owns the sidecar layout, so doctor does not re-derive it.\n3. `src/rebar/_commands/doctor_locks.py`: add `LEG_SNAPSHOT_GC_WORKER = \"snapshot-gc-worker\"`\n   as a sixth leg in `scan_locks`, built by the existing `_existence_report` on\n   `worker_lock_probe_path()` (module imported lazily inside the leg lambda's scope so the\n   census does not import the snapshot subsystem at module import). Note text: \"no detached\n   snapshot-GC worker holds the snapshot store's worker lock (per-host store; may not exist\n   yet)\". Update the module docstring: five → six legs, and a paragraph on the snapshot leg's\n   DIFFERENT root (per-host store, not the tracker), same stamped shape/shared table.\n   `scan_locks(tracker)` keeps its signature; the new leg is per-host and ignores the tracker\n   argument — the docstring says so.\n4. `src/rebar/schemas/doctor.schema.json`: add `\"snapshot-gc-worker\"` to the leg-name enum.\n5. `tests/scripts/graph/test_doctor_locks.py`:\n   - an autouse fixture pinning `REBAR_GATE_TMPDIR` to a per-test tmp dir, so the census's\n     new host-global leg cannot leak REAL host state into any test in the module (the\n     free-store census test and both doctor integration tests assert exact finding sets).\n   - update `test_a_free_store_reports_every_leg_and_no_finding` to six legs; assert the\n     snapshot leg is `free` with `holder is None` when the store does not exist, and that\n     scanning did NOT create the store directory (the read-only guarantee for the new\n     derivation).\n   - `_plant_snapshot_gc_lock` helper writing a v2 stamp at\n     `repo_snapshot.peek_store_root() / \"gc\" / \"worker.lock\"` (under the pinned tmp base);\n     mirror the compact-worker tests: live holder → held/info, dead holder → stale finding\n     via `lock_findings`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] The snapshot-GC worker lock joins `rebar doctor`'s census as leg\n      `snapshot-gc-worker`, derived from the per-host snapshot-store root without creating\n      any directory.\n- [x] The leg reports held-for / holder / staleness like the other stamped legs, with tests\n      for held (live + dead holder) and free/absent store.\n- [x] The dead-holder case is a stale-lock finding; a live holder is information; an absent\n      store (or free lock) is no finding, and the doctor JSON schema admits the new leg name.\n\n## Verify\n- pytest tests/scripts/graph/test_doctor_locks.py tests/unit/test_snapshot_gc_trigger.py tests/unit/snapshot/test_repo_snapshot.py -x -q  (repo_snapshot tests live where they live; adjust path if the module sits directly under tests/unit)\n- make lint; make typecheck; python scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --check\n","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_snapshot/repo_snapshot.py","reason":"add peek_store_root() read-only derivation; store_root() refactored to use it"},{"path":"src/rebar/_snapshot/gc_trigger.py","reason":"hoist _GC_DIRNAME; add worker_lock_probe_path() non-creating seam for doctor"},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/doctor_locks.py","reason":"sixth census leg snapshot-gc-worker via _existence_report; docstring five->six legs"},{"path":"src/rebar/schemas/doctor.schema.json","reason":"admit snapshot-gc-worker in the leg-name enum"},{"path":"tests/scripts/graph/test_doctor_locks.py","reason":"REBAR_GATE_TMPDIR autouse isolation; six-leg census; live/dead/absent-store tests"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","4a87-4da3-1a92-43a9"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"69c3c9b5-f154-4e31-bfbf-83d1c0eb6b87","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"2b09-d231-2152-42d6","ticket_type":"task","title":"doctor lock census has no snapshot-GC worker-lock leg","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["597bde46-179d-4a64-b588-36238e6cf176","9ed7f5e1-1b08-4b44-bbaa-d7bcafd8b17a","5a7e911c-5409-4f69-b71e-fc73a8ee6557","97238f7a-1a49-4052-bf58-93959a568606","f1e34452-fe53-45d8-99aa-74bcbbaf647d","cfb3cfe1-07bd-454b-b40d-fdaf6aff92a5","149cb421-ad7d-4c43-8072-4ac094e9ea60","5b3adc49-2fc3-490b-8441-cb77635f46ef","33cf76bf-6afe-46f2-9f88-b3b1d41a5a07","69c3c9b5-f154-4e31-bfbf-83d1c0eb6b87","98b64f53-62ed-41a0-9be7-25aa12891fa8"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787400233670088001,"uuid":"7721643e-8597-4842-991f-7d587b53bdb1"}